<title>PERU: Peru's Q1 coffee output dips 2.8 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's Q1 coffee output dips 2.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's first quarter coffee production fell 2.8 percent to 4,331 tonnes from 4,456 tonnes in the same period last year, Agriculture Ministry said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Non-decaffeinated coffee exports fell 71.9 percent in the first two months of the year to $5.077 million from $18.064 million in the same period last year, the ministry added.</p>
<p>Peru, whose principal coffee harvest is between April and November, is South America's number four producer after Brazil, Colombia and Ecuador, according to the government.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
